\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Held-out paired performance of proposed rollout ADP versus audited local search. (a) Test $\Delta v$, (b) test graph cost, and (c)--(d) the corresponding shifted-scenario comparisons. Dashed lines denote parity. Rollout ADP wins 28 of 30 test pairs with two numerical ties and wins 17 of 20 shifted pairs with one tie. Insets report paired-bootstrap intervals for the mean difference; coverage success is matched in every panel.}}{11}{figure.66}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:paired-performance}{{5}{11}{Held-out paired performance of proposed rollout ADP versus audited local search. (a) Test $\Delta v$, (b) test graph cost, and (c)--(d) the corresponding shifted-scenario comparisons. Dashed lines denote parity. Rollout ADP wins 28 of 30 test pairs with two numerical ties and wins 17 of 20 shifted pairs with one tie. Insets report paired-bootstrap intervals for the mean difference; coverage success is matched in every panel}{figure.66}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Component and safety audit. (a) Test $\Delta v$ distributions with bootstrap intervals for method means. (b) Mission success exposes the failure of standalone fitted and hand-scaled critics; fixed rollout, local search, and proposed adaptive rollout reach every goal. (c) Minimum sampled clearance above the 2~m margin and (d) peak input for ADP versus local search. Red lines are acceptance limits. Passive drift and uncertainty are not evaluated.}}{12}{figure.72}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:paired-safety}{{6}{12}{Component and safety audit. (a) Test $\Delta v$ distributions with bootstrap intervals for method means. (b) Mission success exposes the failure of standalone fitted and hand-scaled critics; fixed rollout, local search, and proposed adaptive rollout reach every goal. (c) Minimum sampled clearance above the \unit {2}{m} margin and (d) peak input for ADP versus local search. Red lines are acceptance limits. Passive drift and uncertainty are not evaluated}{figure.72}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Illustrative median-effect held-out case. (a) Generated observation-to-observation routes in the LVLH frame; markers are terminal observations and the star is the common initial state. (b) Weighted inspectable coverage versus executed SOOA count. (c) Cumulative physical $\Delta v$. The ADP route reaches the goal after 10 actions; local search uses 11. The selection is post hoc and does not replace the all-scenario inference.}}{12}{figure.75}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:representative-trajectory}{{7}{12}{Illustrative median-effect held-out case. (a) Generated observation-to-observation routes in the LVLH frame; markers are terminal observations and the star is the common initial state. (b) Weighted inspectable coverage versus executed SOOA count. (c) Cumulative physical $\Delta v$. The ADP route reaches the goal after 10 actions; local search uses 11. The selection is post hoc and does not replace the all-scenario inference}{figure.75}{}}
